# UI Engineering (Turki Dairy ERP)

Apply these skills when designing or polishing interfaces:

- **baseline-ui** — typography scale, spacing rhythm, Tailwind consistency
- **fixing-motion-performance** — animate only `transform` and `opacity`; respect `prefers-reduced-motion`
- **fixing-accessibility** — `role="status"`, `aria-live`, focus, contrast on loading states
- **emil-design-eng** — ease-out for entrances; no `transition: all`; loading screens may use subtle motion (rare/first-load)
- **impeccable** — anti-generic aesthetics; brand-aware color; polish without changing behavior

## Loading & waiting

- Full-page splash: brand navy canvas, staggered fade-up, indeterminate progress rail, status semantics
- Inline/table loading: prefer **Skeleton** over spinners when layout is known
- Button/dialog loading: compact **LoadingIndicator**; keep label visible

## Motion rules

- Duration: 160–600ms for UI feedback; linear only for indeterminate progress
- Easing: `cubic-bezier(0.16, 1, 0.3, 1)` for enter; no blur on full-screen surfaces
- Never block interaction longer than necessary; splash is the only full-screen wait state

## Scope

Polish visuals and micro-interactions only — do not change business logic, routes, or data flow unless explicitly asked.
